it non-zero)\n       - R3.3: --nocheck-order disables check entirely\n       - R3.4: --output-delimiter=STRING replaces tab\n     - Non-goals: no sorting of inputs, no locale-aware collation\n\n   - **cmd/comm/main.go** (existing, 169 lines — must be MODIFIED)\n     - Current `options` struct only has `suppress [3]bool` — needs `checkOrder`, `noCheckOrder` bools and `outputDelimiter` string\n     - `parseArgs` (lines 41-67) only handles short flags (-1, -2, -3) — needs to handle `--check-order`, `--nocheck-order`, `--output-delimiter=STRING`\n     - `compare` (lines 100-125) does line comparison but has NO order checking — needs to track previous lines per file and check ordering\n     - `writeLine` (lines 143-162) uses hardcoded `\"\\t\"` — needs to use `opts.outputDelimiter`\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     type options struct {\n         suppress [3]bool\n     }\n     \n     func parseArgs(args []string) (options, string, string, bool) {\n         var opts options\n         var files []string\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             if arg == \"--\" { continue }\n             if strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && arg != \"-\" && !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n                 for _, ch := range arg[1:] {\n                     switch ch {\n                     case '1': opts.suppress[0] = true\n                     case '2': opts.suppress[1] = true\n                     case '3': opts.suppress[2] = true\n                     }\n                 }\n                 continue\n             }\n             files = append(files, arg)\n         }\n         if len(files) != 2 { return opts, \"\", \"\", false }\n         return opts, files[0], files[1], true\n     }\n     \n     func compare(w *bufio.Writer, opts *options, r1, r2 io.Reader) int {\n         s1 := bufio.NewScanner(r1)\n         s2 := bufio.NewScanner(r2)\n         have1 := s1.Scan()\n         have2 := s2.Scan()\n         for have1 && have2 {\n             line1 := s1.Text()\n             line2 := s2.Text()\n             var err error\n             if line1 < line2 {\n                 err = writeLine(w, opts, 1, line1)\n                 have1 = s1.Scan()\n             } else if line2 < line1 {\n                 err = writeLine(w, opts, 2, line2)\n                 have2 = s2.Scan()\n             } else {\n                 err = writeLine(w, opts, 3, line1)\n                 have1 = s1.Scan()\n                 have2 = s2.Scan()\n             }\n             if err != nil { return epipeOr1(err) }\n         }\n         return drain(w, opts, s1, s2, have1, have2)\n     }\n     \n     func writeLine(w *bufio.Writer, opts *options, col int, line string) error {\n         if opts.suppress[col-1] { return nil }\n         tabs := 0\n         for i := 0; i < col-1; i++ {\n             if !opts.suppress[i] { tabs++ }\n         }\n         for i := 0; i < tabs; i++ {\n             if _, err := w.WriteString(\"\\t\"); err != nil { return err }\n         }\n         if _, err := w.WriteString(line); err != nil { return err }\n         return w.WriteByte('\\n')\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/comm/comm_test.go** (existing, 289 lines — must be MODIFIED)\n     - Has ~32 existing differential test cases covering R1.x and R2.x\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gcomm\")`\n     - Creates temp files: file1.txt, file2.txt, empty.txt, single.txt, abc.txt, bdf.txt, all_same.txt, disjoint1.txt, disjoint2.txt, one_line_a/b.txt, caps.txt, lower.txt, multi.txt, multi2.txt, noeol.txt, noeol2.txt\n     - Has TestSIGPIPE and writeFile helper\n     - Needs new test cases for: unsorted input (default warning), --check-order with unsorted input, --nocheck-order with unsorted input, --output-delimiter with various values\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that `parseArgs` currently skips all `--` prefixed args (they fall t